Digital Payment Awareness Website

About the Project

The Digital Payment Awareness Website is designed to educate people about digital payment methods, common online payment frauds, and safe digital payment practices.

It helps users understand how to use digital payments safely and how to respond to suspicious transactions.

Features

- Introduction to digital payments
- Types of digital payments
- Common online payment frauds
- Digital payment safety tips
- Steps to follow if online fraud occurs
- Interactive awareness quiz
- Responsive design for mobile and desktop

Technologies Used

- HTML
- CSS
- JavaScript

How to Run the Project

1. Download or clone the project.
2. Open the project folder.
3. Locate the "index.html" file.
4. Double-click "index.html".
5. The website will open in your web browser.

Project Structure

Digital-Payment-Awareness/
│
├── index.html
├── style.css
├── script.js
└── README.md

Safety Guidelines

- Never share your OTP or UPI PIN.
- Do not click suspicious payment links.
- Verify payment details before sending money.
- Never scan unknown QR codes to receive money.
- Avoid installing unknown remote-access applications.
- Contact your bank and call 1930 if you suspect financial cyber fraud.

Purpose

The main purpose of this project is to create awareness about digital payment methods, online fraud prevention, and secure digital transactions.

Disclaimer

This website is created for educational and awareness purposes only. It does not process payments or collect banking credentials.